            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R2-env-index",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/shelltest/review_bench_test.go:446",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The new tests recover the stub directory with strings.TrimPrefix(env[2], \"STUB_DIR=\"), which depends on STUB_DIR sitting at position 2 of the slice oursFixture returns. The same positional lookup is repeated in the gentle fixture and its RUN-validation subtest. If the fixture's env order changes, the tests fail with a misleading result: the missing-file check passes vacuously, or the lookup hits the wrong variable. The test helper runOurs is also used to run run-gentle.sh, which reads misleadingly. A small helper that finds STUB_DIR by key, or a fixture that returns the stub directory directly, would make the tests safer to maintain.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/shelltest/review_bench_test.go:446"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 10 changed paths in full. The script changes in run-ours.sh and run-gentle.sh are small and symmetrical: one RUN validation line plus the out= expansion. The README and task Log explain the change well.",
              "The RUN validation line is duplicated verbatim across the two scripts. That is acceptable for standalone bench scripts, so I did not report it.",
              "The only maintainability concern is the positional env[2] lookup in the tests, a low-severity suggestion. The JSON result files are generated records with no readability defects."
            ]
          }
        }
