            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Both scripts place the RUN validation first after set -u. It refuses a set-but-invalid RUN (including empty, 0, x and -1) with exit 2 before any command runs, which matches the request.",
              "The out path ${RUN:+/run$RUN} leaves the path unchanged when RUN is unset, so baseline behavior is preserved. RUN=k writes under run\u003ck\u003e, and the tests assert that an earlier run1 is untouched and that the unsuffixed directory is not written.",
              "Tests in engine/shelltest/review_bench_test.go cover, per runner, the RUN=2 isolation, the unset-RUN pin (gentle) and invalid RUN values with no stub calls and no output directory. These are externally observable assertions at the cheapest level.",
              "The remaining files are docs and review records, with no behavioral reliability concerns."
            ]
